MicroDuck Studio and Clip Gen include renderer and motion-editor algorithms
adapted from Microduck Lab:
https://github.com/jonathanhawkins/microduck-lab
Original sources under duck-viewer/:
  components/Duck.tsx
  components/PoseDuck.tsx
  components/Viewer.tsx
  components/AnimPanel.tsx
  lib/rig.ts
  lib/anim.ts
These adapted portions retain the Apache License, Version 2.0 (included in
LICENSE-APACHE-2.0). Original Harness integration code is MIT-licensed (LICENSE).

Modifications by DeepSeek Harness contributors: isolated body-geometry conversion,
model-derived forward kinematics, explicit frame and pose props, bounded joint
and coupled-rig editing, scoped camera interaction, deterministic resource
disposal, and native Cordis plugin integration with declared session stores;
upstream global interaction stores omitted.

Microduck is a Pollen Robotics project. This integration is not affiliated with
or endorsed by Pollen Robotics. Robot geometry and policy assets are supplied by
the configured backend and retain their respective upstream licenses.

